Flagged traditions: ['rec-film-night: 0 without, 7 with rec.filmMoved', 'rec-all-hands: 0 without, 2 with rec.allHands', 'bridge-hour: 0 without, 2 with bridge.invited']
  baked book-circle: from Matthias Oduya; ties None; Mail: Book circle tomorrow, 20:15, the junior common room. Bring a page you liked and read it to us, or just come and listen. There will be cocoa.
  baked bridge-hour: from Captain Odile Marrow; ties None; Mail: Bridge hour tomorrow, 17:15. Juniors are welcome on Deck 1 for a while: the helm, the charts and the view. I'll be there to say hello. Please don't touch anything red.
  baked cook-along: from Lukas Dlamini; ties None; Mail: Cook-along tomorrow at 15:30 at the galley pass. One simple dish. You stir, you taste, you eat it. Aprons provided.
  baked crew-welcome-tea: from The Wren; ties None; Mail: Basil Bramwell came aboard on Sunday's shuttle. New hand's tea tomorrow at 18:40, in the mess. Come and say hello.
  baked department-cup: from Commander Teo Vance; ties {'tally': {'kind': 'cup', 'choices': ['works', 'watch', 'survey', 'bridge', 'commons'], 'mode': 'teams'}, 'decor': 'cupBoard'}; Mail: The department cup is tomorrow, 20:15 in the gym: a rowing relay, one team for each department. I keep the board. The board does not lie.
  baked farewell-supper: from Chef Auda Brennan; ties {'galley': {'meal': 'dinner', 'dish': 'favourite'}, 'decor': 'longTables'}; Mail: Sunday's shuttle takes Theo Teague away from the Wren. Farewell supper tomorrow, 18:00, in the mess. Come and say goodbye properly.
  baked first-fruits: from Tove Cruz; ties {'galley': {'meal': 'dinner', 'dish': 'first-fruits'}, 'garden': 'harvest'}; Mail: The new beds have their first crop. First-fruit supper tomorrow at dinner, 18:15: a bowl on every table in the mess. One each, please. The garden counted.
  baked first-light: from Dev Raman; ties None; Mail: First Light Cocoa tomorrow at 20:00, the bow lounge. Cocoa, the big windows, and where we're going next. New faces especially welcome. Dev Raman
  baked four-weeks-aboard: from The Works team; ties None; Mail: Friday tea tomorrow, 18:40, is a special one: four weeks aboard. Someone in Works has asked the galley for a cake. We're not saying who.
  baked garden-hour: from Tove Cruz; ties {'garden': 'tend'}; Mail: Garden hour tomorrow, 14:00, in the hydroponics garden: watering, tying in and a bit of weeding. No experience needed. The tomatoes won't judge.
  baked harvest-supper: from Chef Auda Brennan; ties {'galley': {'meal': 'dinner', 'dish': 'harvest-supper', 'batch': 60}, 'tally': {'kind': 'harvest-best', 'choices': ['tomatoes', 'beans', 'squash', 'herbs']}, 'decor': 'harvestTables'}; Mail: Harvest supper tomorrow, 18:00, in the mess: long tables and everything from the garden. Vote for the best of the harvest with your token. Pie after.
  baked knit-and-natter: from Zeke Torres; ties None; Mail: Knit and natter tomorrow at 20:00, junior common room. Bring any hobby, or none. I've got spare needles. Lots.
  baked lantern-walk: from Chief Bram Holt; ties {'decor': 'lanternWalk'}; Mail: Lantern walk tomorrow at 20:30. The Watch will dim the promenade, and there are paper lanterns at the lift plaza for anyone who wants one. Walk slowly.
  baked lap-of-the-wren: from Tomas Lind; ties None; Mail: Lap of the Wren at 20:30: one slow walk round the promenade. No pace, no rules, just company.
  baked late-piano: from The music room; ties None; Mail: Late piano tomorrow, 21:45 in the music room, Deck 4. The Captain plays; anyone may listen. Quiet voices, please.
  baked long-breakfast: from Chef Auda Brennan; ties {'galley': {'meal': 'breakfast', 'dish': 'pancakes', 'until': '10:00'}}; Mail: Long breakfast tomorrow: Saturday pancakes in the mess hall until ten. Sleep in. We'll keep the griddle warm.
  baked midtour: from Matthias Oduya; ties None; Mail: Tomorrow is half the year. Midtour, 20:00, in the bow lounge: write a letter to yourself. I'll seal them, and you'll get yours back at Year's end.
  baked name-on-the-beam-new: from Chief Ines Calder; ties None; Mail: Basil joins Works today. After shift, stay in the bay a minute: there's a name going on the beam.
  baked name-on-the-beam: from Chief Ines Calder; ties None; Mail: After shift tomorrow, stay in the bay a minute. There's a beam with a lot of names on it, and room for one more.
  baked new-hands-tea: from Chief Ines Calder; ties None; Mail: Friday tea tomorrow after dinner, 18:40, Works tea corner. It's your first, so it's your new hand's tea. Bring nothing. That's the point.
  baked off-the-tern: from The Wren; ties None; Mail: The Tern brings Basil Bramwell aboard tomorrow at 17:40. Come down to the shuttle bay and say hello.
  baked one-week-aboard: from Chief Ines Calder; ties None; Mail: One week aboard tomorrow. Zeke tells me you haven't broken anything yet. Well done. He'll buy you a tea in the bow lounge at 17:15.
  baked open-door: from Chief Ines Calder; ties None; Mail: Open door, Wednesday at 16:40, the tea corner. Tea's on me. Questions welcome. Complaints, briefly.
  baked open-lab: from Dr. Imra Sato; ties {'decor': 'openLab'}; Mail: Open lab tomorrow, 17:30, Deck 2. The Survey team will show you what we've collected: rocks, ice, dust, and one sample that hums. Ask anything. Touch only what we hand you.
  baked pick-your-own: from Tove Cruz; ties None; Mail: Pick-your-own breakfast tomorrow at 06:15 in the garden. Baskets by the door. Take what's ripe and carry it up.
  baked postcard-night: from Leila Eklund; ties None; Mail: Postcard night tomorrow at 18:45 by the booths. Cards on the table, pens in the pot. The mail run takes them Friday.
  baked reading-corner: from The bow lounge; ties None; Mail: Reading corner on Sunday at 16:00 in the bow lounge. Bring a book, or borrow one. Quiet voices, comfy chairs.
  baked rec-all-hands: from Captain Odile Marrow; ties None; Mail: The Captain's all-hands is tomorrow, 17:45 in the auditorium. A new season, a few thanks, and then dinner. Everyone off duty, please come.
  baked rec-chiefs-talk: from The Wren talks; ties None; Mail: A chief's talk tomorrow, 19:00 in the auditorium. Twenty-five minutes of their department's best story, then questions. Come and ask one.
  baked rec-cup: from Pell Okafor; ties None; Mail: The Lightdisc Cup is tomorrow, 11:30 at the court, in place of Winner Stays On. Pell's bracket is up in the foyer. Play your matches, cheer the rest, and see whose name goes on the Cup board.
  baked rec-dawn-swim: from Rina Deshi; ties None; Mail: Dawn swim tomorrow, 06:15 at the pool. Empty lanes, quiet water, done before the infirmary opens. Rina will be there. She always is.
  baked rec-film-night: from The rec deck; ties None; Mail: Film night tomorrow, 20:00 in the auditorium. The screen comes down, the lights go down, and there's popcorn from the galley.
  baked rec-float-hour: from Matthias Oduya; ties None; Mail: Float hour tomorrow, 21:30 in the float room. Matthias dims the orbs, someone plays something quiet, and nobody talks. Come and drift.
  baked rec-paddle-club: from Chief Bram Holt; ties None; Mail: Paddle club tomorrow, 18:30 in the river hall. Chief Holt takes you round the slow loop. Helmets on, everyone, no exceptions.
  baked rec-regatta: from Chief Bram Holt; ties None; Mail: The river regatta is tomorrow, 09:30 in the river hall. Heats of four round the loop, Chief Holt on the horn, and the winner's pennant over the dock. Watch from the bank, or paddle the fun heat.
  baked rec-slow-stretch: from Dr. Priya Nandakumar; ties None; Mail: Slow stretch tomorrow, 08:00 in the float room. Dr. Nandakumar leads a gentle stretch at a fifth of a g. Bring water. She'll ask.
  baked rec-talent-night: from Lucia Ferreira; ties None; Mail: Talent night tomorrow, 19:30 in the auditorium. Lucia Ferreira hosts and Maeve Volkov runs the lights. Songs, the piano, juggling, whatever you've got. The sign-up sheet's in the foyer.
  baked rec-wall-night: from Tomas Lind; ties None; Mail: Wall night tomorrow, 18:30 at the climbing wall. Tomas will belay. Climb any route, ring the bell at the top, and your name goes on the season's bell board in the foyer.
  baked rec-wren-talk: from The Wren talks; ties None; Mail: Wren talk tomorrow, 19:00 on the auditorium stage. A ring of chairs, tea from the kettle, and one of the crew talking about something they love. Ask anything.
  baked rec-wso: from Pell Okafor; ties None; Mail: Winner Stays On tomorrow, 11:30 at the Lightdisc court. Pell's chalkboard by the gate: write your name, wait your turn, win and stay on. Sandwiches from the grab shelf.
  baked sowing: from Chef Auda Brennan; ties {'garden': 'sow'}; Mail: A new season starts in the garden: Sowing morning tomorrow, 11:45. Everyone plants a seedling. Yours grows as long as you're aboard.
  baked spice-shelf-supper: from Chef Auda Brennan; ties {'galley': {'meal': 'dinner'}}; Mail: Spice shelf supper tomorrow at 18:15. I'm picking three jars from the shelf. Bring a guess, and an appetite.
  baked sunday-table: from Chef Auda Brennan; ties {'galley': {'meal': 'dinner', 'seating': 'friends', 'side': 'tasting'}, 'decor': 'longTables'}; Mail: Sunday long table tomorrow at 18:00: the tables pushed together, the dish you voted for, and Wednesday's tasting winner on the side. Sit with your people.
  baked sunrise-stretch: from Rina Deshi; ties None; Mail: Sunrise stretch at 06:30, in the garden. Gentle, slow, done before breakfast. Come in what you slept in.
  baked talent-night: from Mira Dahl; ties {'decor': 'talentStage'}; Mail: Talent night tomorrow, 20:15 in the bow lounge. Sing, play, juggle, read a poem, or just clap loudly. Sign up at the bar.
  baked tap-night: from The bow lounge bar; ties None; Mail: Tap night tomorrow at 20:00 in the bow lounge. New drink of the week. Bring a friend and a guess what's in it.
  baked tasting-table: from Chef Auda Brennan; ties {'galley': {'meal': 'dinner', 'extra': 'tasting', 'batch': 20}, 'decor': 'tastingTable', 'tally': {'kind': 'tasting', 'choices': ['herb-flatbread', 'pickled-beans', 'tomato-jam-oatcakes', 'root-crisps', 'miso-greens', 'bean-fritters', 'carrot-ginger-soup', 'chilli-lime-corn'], 'per': 2}}; Mail: Tasting table tomorrow at dinner, from 18:15: two small new dishes by the servery. Try both, drop your token in a jar. The winner comes back on Sunday.
  baked tiles-ladder: from Olu Farouk; ties {'decor': 'tilesNight'}; Mail: Tiles ladder tomorrow at 15:00 in the bow lounge. Everyone plays everyone. The winner's name goes on the chalkboard.
  baked tiles-night: from Rina Deshi; ties {'decor': 'tilesNight'}; Mail: Tiles night tomorrow, 20:00 in the bow lounge. A board on every table. Beginners welcome; my title is not up for discussion.
  baked years-end: from Captain Odile Marrow; ties {'decor': 'yearsEnd'}; Mail: Tomorrow is the year's last evening. Bow lounge, 20:00: I'll read a little from the log, and Matthias has your Midtour letters. Come as you are.
